    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "I really appreciate you sharing that story. I agree with you. I feel like the moment is calling for people, there's the whole idea that silence is violence. And I know also with sexual harassment, many times people kept their mouth shut because they thought that was the safer thing to do. But in fact, it's just perpetuated perpetration. I really relate when people are saying silence is violence because we need bystanders to come forward and be witness and hold that space for people and say, yeah, I see that. I see what happened to you. I'm acknowledging that. And yes, while I haven't experienced it myself, I saw it happen to you and I'm not going to negate your reality.",
