  {
    "episode_id": 95507,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95507.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I think that is a huge growing problem. And that is part of our job, our committee and then the Appropriations Committee that actually appropriates how much money goes to each agency. But we've seen a dramatic upsurge of hate groups using social media. We've seen even recently in the last week or so, like in Albuquerque, some of these hate groups. actually fire on protesters. What's amazing is Donald Trump says this must all be groups on the left like Antifa, at least so far. The documentation that I'm seeing both in public and private is that it's much more that kind of boogaloo and some of these groups on the right than it is groups on the left. Now again, I'm sure there are hate groups on both ends of the political But what we ought to be making our decisions on is what the data shows, not just what Mr. Trump tweets out. I think if you look at the data from the FBI, and there's even been public reporting on this, the vast majority in the recent weeks have come from Brugalou and other type right-wing groups, and that with people today and said, this is about our national security. We need to have, just as we've seen any other kind of terrorist group needs to be monitored, these are terrorist groups.",
