    "turn_text": "Yeah, I also saw something that I guess in the Seattle Times, there was a picture that someone from Fox, it was a doctored photograph. And so, you know, when you superimpose images onto a photograph, it's really not, it's not photojournalism, but people see it and they see this image and they get so reactive. And somehow they're getting away with it by calling it art or something. I don't know.",
