  {
    "episode_id": 95507,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95507.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, this is like one of the scariest things, especially as we go into these last couple of months before elections, you know, in a That's not just the news, but you see this. I know out in Hollywood a lot, which called deep fakes, where you can suddenly put the visual image of somebody's head on somebody else's body. You can make somebody look like they're doing or saying anything. And in a world we're seeing is still believing as this technology gets better and better, the ability to have false images put in front of your face. We've seen it again in Hollywood, oftentimes around actually my understanding kind of around actors being put in sex videos or other things that are not actors or actresses that are not those people. It could happen in politics. It could happen in business. What happens if you put an image of the chairman of the Federal Reserve on a body and makes it sound like it's saying Federal Reserve is going to launch this big problem. You could cost billions of dollars and that kind of lack of having rules around some of this technology, I think is gonna come back and bite us. And, you know, we have to approach it thoughtfully, but it is a big, big issue. And I think we've been actually lucky that it hasn't caused more problem already this whole issue around deep fakes. What can we do? Part of it means informed consumers, part of it means that this question of trying to have some trusted sites, part of it means having some rules where we don't just rely upon the good graces of Facebook and Twitter and YouTube to be the police. that they actually are some rules. There's something called Section 230 that is in the law that the federal communication law basically allows these things. Sometimes if there are no responsibility, if they post things totally false or inciting a violence, if somebody incites violence, and then that violence takes place, you know, at some level, there needs to be some",
